1159
01:11:48,110 --> 01:11:49,390
Where's Saria, though?

1160
01:12:00,720 --> 01:12:01,820
Chamber of the Sages.

1161
01:12:03,620 --> 01:12:04,340
Wow!

1162
01:12:04,780 --> 01:12:06,300
I got teleported here immediately.

1163
01:12:12,490 --> 01:12:13,710
There she is!

1164
01:12:14,790 --> 01:12:15,630
Thank you!

1165
01:12:16,270 --> 01:12:18,730
Because of you, I could awaken a sage.

1166
01:12:20,950 --> 01:12:24,550
I am Saria, the sage of the Forest Temple.

1167
01:12:26,130 --> 01:12:26,750
What?

1168
01:12:27,070 --> 01:12:28,010
You got promoted!

1169
01:12:30,730 --> 01:12:32,710
I always believed that you would come.

1170
01:12:33,050 --> 01:12:34,310
Because I know you.

1171
01:12:35,570 --> 01:12:35,910
No.

1172
01:12:37,010 --> 01:12:39,010
You don't have to explain it to me.

1173
01:12:40,550 --> 01:12:43,930
Because it is destiny that you and I can't live in the same world.

1174
01:12:43,930 --> 01:12:45,230
No, Saria!

1175
01:12:45,310 --> 01:12:45,950
Don't say that!

1176
01:12:48,850 --> 01:12:51,350
I will stay here as the Forest Sage and help you.

1177
01:12:52,370 --> 01:12:54,490
Now, please take this medallion.

1178
01:13:14,520 --> 01:13:15,500
It's a medal.

1179
01:13:16,340 --> 01:13:16,900
Leon.

1180
01:13:17,880 --> 01:13:19,000
Forest medal, Leon.

1181
01:13:19,760 --> 01:13:22,880
Saria awakens as a sage and adds her power to yours.

1182
01:13:23,800 --> 01:13:25,500
Okay, but what power is that?

1183
01:13:27,780 --> 01:13:29,680
Saria will always be your friend.

1184
01:13:29,840 --> 01:13:30,300
Oh my god.

1185
01:13:31,000 --> 01:13:32,020
I've been sown.

1186
01:13:51,970 --> 01:13:53,110
Don't smell it, Link.

1187
01:13:53,250 --> 01:13:53,450
Oh!

1188
01:13:53,930 --> 01:13:54,270
Oh!

1189
01:14:01,420 --> 01:14:02,000
Hi there!

1190
01:14:02,580 --> 01:14:04,260
I'm the Deku Tree Sprout!

1191
01:14:05,300 --> 01:14:10,000
Because you and Saria broke the curse on the Forest Temple, I can grow and flourish!

1192
01:14:10,980 --> 01:14:11,880
Thanks a lot!

1193
01:14:13,040 --> 01:14:13,580
Okay.

1194
01:14:16,460 --> 01:14:18,140
Hey, are you seeing your old friends?

1195
01:14:18,540 --> 01:14:21,520
None of them recognized you with your grown-up body, did they?

1196
01:14:22,840 --> 01:14:24,880
That's because the Kokiri never grow up!

1197
01:14:25,120 --> 01:14:27,300
Even after seven years, they're still kids!

1198
01:14:30,040 --> 01:14:32,540
You must be wondering why only you have grown up.

1199
01:14:33,700 --> 01:14:35,280
I think I know the answer to that.

1200
01:14:35,480 --> 01:14:38,640
Well, as you might have already guessed, you're not a Kokiri.

1201
01:14:39,580 --> 01:14:41,040
You're actually a Hylian!

1202
01:14:42,100 --> 01:14:42,580
Really?

1203
01:14:43,240 --> 01:14:45,640
I'm happy to finally reveal this secret to you!

1204
01:14:47,800 --> 01:14:48,280
Thanks!

1205
01:14:51,650 --> 01:14:54,170
But, so the fairy was a lie all this time?

1206
01:14:54,930 --> 01:15:00,230
Some time ago, before the King of Hyrule unified this country, there was a fierce war in our world.

1207
01:15:02,930 --> 01:15:09,730
One day, to escape from the fires of the war, a Hylian mother and her baby boy entered this forbidden forest.

1208
01:15:13,140 --> 01:15:14,960
The mother was gravely injured.

1209
01:15:15,360 --> 01:15:20,540
Her only choice was to entrust the child to the Deku Tree, the guardian spirit of the forest.

1210
01:15:24,500 --> 01:15:32,060
The Deku Tree could sense that this was a child of destiny, whose fate would affect the entire world, so he took him into the forest.

1211
01:15:36,230 --> 01:15:42,590
After the mother passed away, the baby was raised as a Kokiri, and now, finally, the day of destiny has come.

1212
01:15:43,670 --> 01:15:44,770
Nooo, she's dead!

1213
01:15:50,890 --> 01:15:54,490
You are a Hylian, and were always bound to leave this forest!

1214
01:15:55,450 --> 01:16:00,050
And now, you have learned your own destiny, so you know what you must do!

1215
01:16:00,930 --> 01:16:04,050
That's right, you must save the land of Hyrule!

1216
01:16:05,070 --> 01:16:10,330
Now, Link, break the curses of all the temples, and return peace to Hyrule!

1217
01:16:12,990 --> 01:16:15,690
All right, weirdo, I will.

1218
01:16:18,500 --> 01:16:22,920
Hi there, I'm the Deku Tree Sprout, because you and Saria broke!

1219
01:16:28,300 --> 01:16:29,500
See you later, man!

1220
01:16:30,480 --> 01:16:31,440
See you later!

1221
01:16:35,120 --> 01:16:36,560
Oh, that's funny!

1222
01:16:37,600 --> 01:16:38,900
Let me go boing boing!

1223
01:16:40,300 --> 01:16:41,000
Boing it!

1224
01:16:43,040 --> 01:16:43,600
Whoa!

1225
01:16:43,840 --> 01:16:44,100
Wow!

1226
01:16:45,200 --> 01:16:46,160
What a time!

1227
01:16:46,900 --> 01:16:48,120
That means it's lunch!

1228
01:16:49,160 --> 01:16:50,040
Lunch time!

1229
01:16:50,660 --> 01:16:52,600
I wonder what the people of the Kokiri Forest eat.

1230
01:16:52,880 --> 01:16:54,900
I bet they eat baby sprouts!

1231
01:16:56,500 --> 01:16:57,720
Look how scared he is!

1232
01:16:57,920 --> 01:16:58,900
He knows he's next!

1233
01:17:01,080 --> 01:17:01,800
That's right!

1234
01:17:02,360 --> 01:17:03,700
I'm gonna eat you!

1235
01:17:06,530 --> 01:17:08,290
Well, I'm gonna cook you first, but...

1236
01:17:08,930 --> 01:17:09,990
Then I will eat you.

1237
01:17:10,710 --> 01:17:12,650
Let's go back to the Kokiri Forest here.

1238
01:17:20,040 --> 01:17:21,880
I can't get over Link's fake legs.

1239
01:17:24,220 --> 01:17:25,080
It ain't real.

1240
01:17:26,640 --> 01:17:27,720
Nice stilts, nerd.

1241
01:17:30,300 --> 01:17:31,980
Just ahead, great Deku Tree's meadow.

1242
01:17:34,120 --> 01:17:34,940
What do you want to say?

1243
01:17:35,480 --> 01:17:37,860
I feel like I've known you for a long time, mister.

1244
01:17:38,360 --> 01:17:38,940
Well, you have.

1245
01:17:39,540 --> 01:17:41,520
Also, let me call my, uh...

1246
01:17:41,520 --> 01:17:42,860
Well, friend, I guess.

1247
01:17:45,480 --> 01:17:46,220
Oh wait, wait a minute.

1248
01:17:46,320 --> 01:17:47,340
I'm the only one that has aged.

1249
01:17:50,460 --> 01:17:51,600
That explains a lot!

1250
01:17:53,200 --> 01:17:54,560
In fact, that explains everything.

1251
01:17:55,620 --> 01:17:55,900
Huh.

1252
01:18:05,800 --> 01:18:07,080
You want to talk to Saria, right?

1253
01:18:07,440 --> 01:18:08,660
Yeah, I want to talk to her.

1254
01:18:09,200 --> 01:18:09,500
Link!

1255
01:18:09,800 --> 01:18:11,140
This is Saria, can you hear me?

1256
01:18:11,180 --> 01:18:12,160
I can always hear you.

1257
01:18:12,320 --> 01:18:13,760
There's never been a problem with this device.

1258
01:18:15,040 --> 01:18:17,420
At first, I didn't want to become the Sage of the Forest.

1259
01:18:18,900 --> 01:18:20,140
But I'm glad now.

1260
01:18:21,300 --> 01:18:23,420
Because I am helping you to save Hyrule.

1261
01:18:23,720 --> 01:18:23,780
Link!

1262
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:24,800
Yes, I am!

1263
01:18:25,940 --> 01:18:27,680
You want to talk to Saria again?

1264
01:18:28,060 --> 01:18:28,840
No, I'm good.

1265
01:18:29,760 --> 01:18:32,580
She is a woman of few words, I would say.

1266
01:18:33,180 --> 01:18:34,820
She never does say much, does she?

1267
01:18:35,100 --> 01:18:35,760
Oh, dude!

1268
01:18:36,160 --> 01:18:37,180
We should buy arrows!

1269
01:18:38,200 --> 01:18:39,520
Or maybe I get arrows here.

1270
01:18:45,460 --> 01:18:46,360
I get bombs!

1271
01:18:48,320 --> 01:18:49,080
Actually sick.

1272
01:18:49,860 --> 01:18:50,640
But you know what?

1273
01:18:50,660 --> 01:18:51,580
I will buy some arrows.

1274
01:18:52,380 --> 01:18:56,520
Because, uh, I feel bad picking up a bunch of rupees when I already have full, you know?

1275
01:18:57,680 --> 01:18:59,000
Um, you.

1276
01:19:00,080 --> 01:19:01,320
Your little medicine man.

1277
01:19:02,020 --> 01:19:03,260
Let me buy some of these arrows.

1278
01:19:03,840 --> 01:19:04,600
30 pieces!

1279
01:19:06,200 --> 01:19:07,420
10 pieces, hmm.

1280
01:19:08,900 --> 01:19:12,080
I thought that would be a discount on three, but I guess not.

1281
01:19:12,240 --> 01:19:13,200
Three times this, but yeah.

1282
01:19:14,300 --> 01:19:17,380
Let's buy, uh, this.

1283
01:19:18,720 --> 01:19:19,620
Let's buy two of them.

1284
01:19:21,940 --> 01:19:23,360
We're gonna get the rest somewhere else.

1285
01:19:24,680 --> 01:19:28,620
Because, as they say, all these stuff, uh, or things can be found in the forest, right?

1286
01:19:35,650 --> 01:19:36,710
I think I just found some arrows.

1287
01:19:36,870 --> 01:19:36,950
Yeah.

1288
01:19:37,590 --> 01:19:37,930
Beautiful!

1289
01:19:40,370 --> 01:19:41,370
Now we're full on that.

1290
01:19:42,150 --> 01:19:46,730
Uh, we would like to have some more nuts and some more, um, bonds.

1291
01:19:46,730 --> 01:19:46,850
Nice.

1292
01:19:51,030 --> 01:19:52,350
Teach me some fancy fencing.

1293
01:19:52,530 --> 01:19:54,750
All I've ever done is tap B all my life.

1294
01:19:56,050 --> 01:19:56,710
Uh, B.

1295
01:20:01,250 --> 01:20:01,770
Wait a minute.

1296
01:20:01,970 --> 01:20:03,510
I, for some reason I have a brain for it right now.

1297
01:20:04,030 --> 01:20:06,170
The attack button has never been this button, has it?

1298
01:20:06,390 --> 01:20:07,970
Wait, am I imagining things?

1299
01:20:10,210 --> 01:20:10,570
Huh.

1300
01:20:12,370 --> 01:20:14,230
I swear to god, sometimes I'm like, wait, what?

1301
01:20:15,650 --> 01:20:17,530
I guess it was this, the button all the time.

1302
01:20:18,110 --> 01:20:18,890
That's just weird.

1303
01:20:20,850 --> 01:20:21,570
What about you?

1304
01:20:22,510 --> 01:20:27,530
Now that the Deku Tree's sprout is growing in the Great Deku Tree's meadow, the forest has returned to normal.

1305
01:20:28,230 --> 01:20:30,990
Oh yeah, actually, I noticed no more evil creatures here.

1306
01:20:31,510 --> 01:20:32,270
Good stuff.

1307
01:20:33,130 --> 01:20:34,450
Let me go talk to more people.

1308
01:20:35,430 --> 01:20:36,530
I want to hear their opinion.

1309
01:20:36,630 --> 01:20:37,670
I also want to go do some gardening.

1310
01:20:39,910 --> 01:20:42,050
Bombs and gold.

1311
01:20:43,330 --> 01:20:44,310
That's what I'm after.

1312
01:20:45,890 --> 01:20:46,350
Uh,

1313
01:20:52,200 --> 01:20:52,360
you.

1314
01:20:53,940 --> 01:20:56,680
Somehow, a fair wind has begun to blow recently.

1315
01:20:58,660 --> 01:20:59,720
Yeah, it's because of...

1316
01:20:59,720 --> 01:21:01,000
Oh my god, look how tall I am!

1317
01:21:02,500 --> 01:21:04,020
I barely fit in this hut!

1318
01:21:04,140 --> 01:21:05,000
I feel like a giant!

1319
01:21:07,140 --> 01:21:08,220
Oh my god, it's weird.

1320
01:21:10,420 --> 01:21:12,220
I'm sure Link will return someday.

1321
01:21:12,940 --> 01:21:13,920
I'm right here.

1322
01:21:15,240 --> 01:21:18,860
Since a fair wind started to blow, I'm sure Link will come back!

1323
01:21:19,780 --> 01:21:21,440
You are more right than you think.

1324
01:21:22,760 --> 01:21:23,900
Why can't I put this up?

1325
01:21:24,020 --> 01:21:24,420
Oh, there we go.

1326
01:21:25,980 --> 01:21:27,160
Let me just break your shit.

1327
01:21:30,090 --> 01:21:31,230
I can't reach those.

1328
01:21:33,590 --> 01:21:34,890
I guess those are lost.

1329
01:21:36,850 --> 01:21:37,930
What do you mean a fair wind?

1330
01:21:38,010 --> 01:21:38,950
Is that because of the sprout?

1331
01:21:40,950 --> 01:21:41,810
A fair wind?

1332
01:21:41,970 --> 01:21:42,930
Let me go inside my house.

1333
01:21:43,570 --> 01:21:44,970
We gotta check something real quick.

1334
01:21:45,230 --> 01:21:46,630
We can see statistics in here.

1335
01:21:48,930 --> 01:21:49,870
And I wanna know.

1336
01:21:54,780 --> 01:21:56,040
21 spiders squished!

1337
01:21:56,500 --> 01:21:59,440
That's gotta be a threshold for the next one, right?

1338
01:22:01,830 --> 01:22:03,090
Oh, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow.

1339
01:22:03,210 --> 01:22:05,110
We gotta go back to the village.

1340
01:22:08,250 --> 01:22:09,290
Let me also see the map.

1341
01:22:09,370 --> 01:22:10,370
What is my next step here?

1342
01:22:11,270 --> 01:22:12,290
I actually have a bunch.

1343
01:22:12,290 --> 01:22:13,210
I can choose.

1344
01:22:15,430 --> 01:22:15,970
I can choose.

1345
01:22:15,970 --> 01:22:16,750
Lon Lon Ranch.

1346
01:22:17,430 --> 01:22:18,310
Death Mountain.

1347
01:22:18,570 --> 01:22:20,270
I can't even speak.

1348
01:22:20,450 --> 01:22:21,750
Kakariko is a good place.

1349
01:22:22,130 --> 01:22:23,150
I wanna go there.

1350
01:22:25,850 --> 01:22:27,930
Is there anyone else I need to speak to here?

1351
01:22:28,690 --> 01:22:29,930
Maybe the bad guy.

1352
01:22:31,050 --> 01:22:31,590
Mito.

1353
01:22:38,100 --> 01:22:38,900
He's gone!

1354
01:22:41,320 --> 01:22:42,500
Where did he go?

1355
01:22:44,080 --> 01:22:44,620
Huh.

1356
01:22:45,960 --> 01:22:46,520
Interesting.

1357
01:22:48,020 --> 01:22:49,040
Who's this down here?

1358
01:22:51,780 --> 01:22:52,340
Link!

1359
01:22:52,720 --> 01:22:54,500
I wonder if he will ever come back.

1360
01:22:55,480 --> 01:22:56,400
Yeah, me too.

1361
01:23:02,200 --> 01:23:03,540
The cuckoo sinks.

1362
01:23:04,320 --> 01:23:05,140
It's morning.

1363
01:23:05,420 --> 01:23:07,620
And what a beautiful morning it is in Hyrule field.

1364
01:23:09,680 --> 01:23:11,000
We're going straight to...

1365
01:23:11,540 --> 01:23:12,160
So hold on.

1366
01:23:12,840 --> 01:23:14,660
The castle is fucked right now, right?

1367
01:23:14,780 --> 01:23:15,800
Everything is burned over there.

1368
01:23:16,000 --> 01:23:16,920
It's all horrible.

1369
01:23:20,220 --> 01:23:21,240
It's still like that, right?

1370
01:23:22,520 --> 01:23:24,280
Why does all that feel like a distant dream?

1371
01:23:25,620 --> 01:23:26,860
It looks fine from here.

1372
01:23:29,640 --> 01:23:31,520
Are things really still messed up in there?

1373
01:23:33,320 --> 01:23:34,180
I guess so.

1374
01:23:36,260 --> 01:23:38,580
We're gonna go to Lon Lon Ranch and grab a bunch of milk.

1375
01:23:40,100 --> 01:23:40,660
Oh yeah.

1376
01:23:41,260 --> 01:23:42,260
We're gonna be milking.

1377
01:23:49,660 --> 01:23:52,580
Imagine how useful that milk would have been during that boss fight.

1378
01:23:52,840 --> 01:23:55,300
I could have actually one-shot him, you know?

1379
01:23:55,380 --> 01:23:56,100
If I had the milk.

1380
01:23:57,540 --> 01:23:58,280
Cheers to that.

1381
01:24:11,170 --> 01:24:12,450
Lon Lon Ranch.

1382
01:24:12,450 --> 01:24:14,070
Uh, let's check out this.

1383
01:24:22,250 --> 01:24:23,010
Go upstairs.

1384
01:24:30,440 --> 01:24:32,940
I also want to talk to, um, Malon.

1385
01:24:33,240 --> 01:24:35,300
Now that we woke, uh, her father up again.

1386
01:24:35,640 --> 01:24:36,360
Maybe something happens.

1387
01:24:37,360 --> 01:24:37,780
Oh,

1388
01:24:41,040 --> 01:24:42,040
I can actually grab it.

1389
01:24:42,120 --> 01:24:42,460
That's sick.

1390
01:24:44,020 --> 01:24:45,240
I thought it was lost forever.

1391
01:24:48,380 --> 01:24:50,240
That evil laugh gets me every time.

1392
01:24:51,060 --> 01:24:52,860
You cannot tell me that's not an evil laugh.

1393
01:25:02,050 --> 01:25:03,110
It's cow time!

1394
01:25:05,090 --> 01:25:06,210
Check it out, buddy.

1395
01:25:06,630 --> 01:25:07,630
Let me see if I remember this.

1396
01:25:18,460 --> 01:25:19,160
Is that it?

1397
01:25:22,660 --> 01:25:23,660
I can't remember.

1398
01:25:23,980 --> 01:25:24,500
Yes!

1399
01:25:24,680 --> 01:25:25,040
I did it!

1400
01:25:26,420 --> 01:25:26,940
Yeah!

1401
01:25:28,180 --> 01:25:29,100
Fill it up!

1402
01:25:31,220 --> 01:25:31,740
Amazing.

1403
01:25:33,040 --> 01:25:33,880
One more time.

1404
01:25:39,020 --> 01:25:39,540
No!

1405
01:25:39,920 --> 01:25:41,260
I didn't mean to play that!

1406
01:25:42,180 --> 01:25:42,580
Whoops!

1407
01:25:45,960 --> 01:25:48,060
Also, I just want to check something real quick.

1408
01:25:50,620 --> 01:25:51,980
Okay, so it filled one bottle.

1409
01:25:52,520 --> 01:25:55,400
Maybe I'll leave one bottle empty in case I need to grab something, you know?

1410
01:25:55,640 --> 01:25:56,500
Like a fish.

1411
01:25:57,260 --> 01:25:59,000
Uh, I actually forgot the melody again.

1412
01:25:59,080 --> 01:25:59,540
It's insane.

1413
01:26:01,220 --> 01:26:01,920
What was it?

1414
01:26:02,840 --> 01:26:03,700
Bup, bup, bup.

1415
01:26:16,670 --> 01:26:17,390
That's right!

1416
01:26:17,830 --> 01:26:18,630
Fill me up!

1417
01:26:21,290 --> 01:26:21,730
Thanks!

1418
01:26:22,730 --> 01:26:24,790
Oh, Jesus Christ, lady!

1419
01:26:26,770 --> 01:26:27,950
You came out of nowhere!

1420
01:26:28,710 --> 01:26:29,950
Oh, a visitor!

1421
01:26:30,650 --> 01:26:33,110
It's been a long time since we've had a visitor here.

1422
01:26:33,590 --> 01:26:34,750
Where did you come from?

1423
01:26:36,570 --> 01:26:43,630
Since Ganondorf came, people in the castle town have gone, places have been ruined, and monsters are wandering everywhere.

1424
01:26:44,670 --> 01:26:47,850
Mr. Ingo was just using the ranch to gain Ganondorf's favor.

1425
01:26:48,190 --> 01:26:48,990
I knew it!

1426
01:26:49,050 --> 01:26:52,490
That guy is a messy person who needs to be punished.

1427
01:26:53,610 --> 01:26:55,230
Everyone seems to be turning evil.

1428
01:26:56,170 --> 01:26:59,770
But Dad, he was kicked out of the ranch by Mr. Ingo.

1429
01:27:00,810 --> 01:27:04,230
If I disobey Mr. Ingo, he will treat the horses so badly.

1430
01:27:04,790 --> 01:27:06,070
Not on my watch!

1431
01:27:07,230 --> 01:27:09,030
So, there's nothing I can do!

1432
01:27:10,590 --> 01:27:16,690
I will go murder Mr. Ingo right now, and reinstate your dad as the rightful owner of Lon Lon Ranch.

1433
01:27:17,610 --> 01:27:18,450
You hear me?

1434
01:27:19,270 --> 01:27:22,390
But after breakfast, right now, I just gotta, you know.

1435
01:27:23,150 --> 01:27:23,430
Kidding.

1436
01:27:24,390 --> 01:27:24,830
Kidding.

1437
01:27:25,490 --> 01:27:25,930
I've...

1438
01:27:25,930 --> 01:27:26,710
Didn't we just...

1439
01:27:26,710 --> 01:27:27,170
Okay.

1440
01:27:28,330 --> 01:27:29,790
Um, I will figure it out.

1441
01:27:32,030 --> 01:27:33,070
I'll figure it out.

1442
01:27:40,600 --> 01:27:41,920
Is that Mr. Ingo?

1443
01:27:44,700 --> 01:27:46,160
Wait a minute, that horse has a saddle.

1444
01:27:46,380 --> 01:27:47,400
Does that mean I can ride it?

1445
01:27:49,760 --> 01:27:54,860
There are some people in Kakariko spreading rumors that I cheated Talon out of the ranch, but...

1446
01:27:55,460 --> 01:27:56,820
Don't be ridiculous.

1447
01:27:57,760 --> 01:27:59,480
That guy Talon was weak.

1448
01:28:00,300 --> 01:28:04,200
I, the heart-working Ingo, poured so much energy into this place.

1449
01:28:05,060 --> 01:28:08,660
I don't want any strangers like you saying anything bad about me.

1450
01:28:09,820 --> 01:28:10,340
Listen.

1451
01:28:10,880 --> 01:28:15,080
The great Ganondorf recognized my obvious talons and gave the ranch to me.

1452
01:28:15,940 --> 01:28:16,620
Oh yeah?

1453
01:28:16,840 --> 01:28:17,640
You suck up!

1454
01:28:18,380 --> 01:28:22,360
I will raise a fine horse and win recognition from the great Ganondorf.

1455
01:28:23,440 --> 01:28:26,980
Say, young man, do you want to ride one of my fine horses?

1456
01:28:28,080 --> 01:28:30,200
Pay me ten rupees and you can ride.

1457
01:28:30,880 --> 01:28:32,300
Oh hell yeah, that's nothing.

1458
01:28:33,660 --> 01:28:35,200
Do you want to hear how to ride?

1459
01:28:36,600 --> 01:28:37,040
Okay.

1460
01:28:38,420 --> 01:28:41,500
Approach the horse quietly and stand by its side.

1461
01:28:41,880 --> 01:28:43,160
Press A to mount up.

1462
01:28:44,000 --> 01:28:45,640
Use the stick to make it run.

1463
01:28:46,080 --> 01:28:48,760
Once it starts running, press A to tap it with the whip.

1464
01:28:49,140 --> 01:28:50,220
It will speed up.

1465
01:28:51,100 --> 01:28:55,080
When you want to jump over a fence, accelerate and hit it head on.

1466
01:28:56,720 --> 01:29:01,480
Uh, if you try to jump over a fence at an angle, the horse won't like it and it won't jump.

1467
01:29:02,920 --> 01:29:10,060
In other words, we as developers did not account for the not-straight-on attack, you know?

1468
01:29:11,200 --> 01:29:14,260
After the horse comes to a complete stop, press A to dismount.

1469
01:29:14,260 --> 01:29:15,360
Now have fun.

1470
01:29:16,820 --> 01:29:18,120
Thank you so much!

1471
01:29:19,620 --> 01:29:20,560
Evil man.

1472
01:29:23,120 --> 01:29:24,260
Oh, there's a timer?

1473
01:29:37,610 --> 01:29:38,230
Link?

1474
01:29:42,260 --> 01:29:42,620
Yes!

1475
01:29:43,400 --> 01:29:44,620
Wait, what am I supposed to do here?

1476
01:29:46,340 --> 01:29:47,240
How do I get points?

1477
01:29:54,950 --> 01:29:56,310
It can't jump over the big one.

1478
01:30:01,540 --> 01:30:02,700
Maybe we need more speed.

1479
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:15,400
Shit!

1480
01:30:21,330 --> 01:30:22,150
Oh my god.

1481
01:30:23,390 --> 01:30:24,990
I'm not sure what I was supposed to do.

1482
01:30:26,610 --> 01:30:28,010
Uh, you only paid 10 rupees.

1483
01:30:28,190 --> 01:30:29,210
You played around long enough.

1484
01:30:29,390 --> 01:30:29,710
Um.

1485
01:30:35,490 --> 01:30:36,950
Can I jump over the big one?

1486
01:30:47,900 --> 01:30:48,480
Wait a minute.

1487
01:30:58,820 --> 01:31:00,000
Maybe that will encourage it.

1488
01:31:05,210 --> 01:31:06,010
Oh no, okay.

1489
01:31:06,570 --> 01:31:07,830
I thought she loved that song.

1490
01:31:08,370 --> 01:31:09,390
Let me do it one more time.

1491
01:31:11,410 --> 01:31:12,130
One more time.

1492
01:31:17,490 --> 01:31:18,030
Come on.

1493
01:31:19,830 --> 01:31:20,770
Get me going again.

1494
01:31:26,820 --> 01:31:27,960
Wait, I can also shoot?

1495
01:31:32,820 --> 01:31:33,220
Oh!

1496
01:31:34,160 --> 01:31:35,600
Wait, am I supposed to...

1497
01:31:40,940 --> 01:31:42,360
Wait, there's also another horse over here.

1498
01:31:45,780 --> 01:31:47,000
I am so confused!

1499
01:31:49,800 --> 01:31:51,160
I don't know what I'm supposed to do.

1500
01:31:52,380 --> 01:31:53,300
I'm shooting horses.

1501
01:31:53,540 --> 01:31:54,620
It's the only target I have.

1502
01:31:55,360 --> 01:31:56,240
How about we shoot this guy?

1503
01:32:03,640 --> 01:32:04,000
Oh!

1504
01:32:15,070 --> 01:32:17,130
Bro, I don't understand what's happening.

1505
01:32:20,430 --> 01:32:22,410
Maybe I need to jump over this a certain amount of times.

1506
01:32:26,830 --> 01:32:28,290
Okay, I don't know what's going on.

1507
01:32:29,470 --> 01:32:30,910
I mean, I have plenty of money.

1508
01:32:31,050 --> 01:32:32,110
I can keep doing this forever.

1509
01:32:34,770 --> 01:32:36,030
What if I play you the melody?

1510
01:32:51,970 --> 01:32:52,550
Come on!

1511
01:32:53,830 --> 01:32:55,110
Yeah, let me hear it once more.

1512
01:32:55,450 --> 01:32:56,130
Oh, go!

1513
01:32:56,290 --> 01:32:57,410
No, I didn't need to skip that!

1514
01:32:59,550 --> 01:33:02,250
After the horse comes to a complete stop, press A to dismount.

1515
01:33:03,570 --> 01:33:04,830
I mean, there's another horse in there.

1516
01:33:09,280 --> 01:33:10,560
Let me go ride this one instead.

1517
01:33:11,460 --> 01:33:12,280
Maybe that will jump over.

1518
01:33:13,000 --> 01:33:13,360
Hey!

1519
01:33:17,100 --> 01:33:17,620
Come here!

1520
01:33:24,270 --> 01:33:25,850
Let me target you so I can...

1521
01:33:27,410 --> 01:33:28,510
I need to target you!

1522
01:33:29,750 --> 01:33:31,470
Maybe he will stand still when I do it.

1523
01:33:32,070 --> 01:33:32,270
Now!

1524
01:33:32,670 --> 01:33:34,230
Okay, I'm right near its ass.

1525
01:33:36,910 --> 01:33:37,610
Calm down!

1526
01:33:46,060 --> 01:33:46,920
There we go!

1527
01:33:47,260 --> 01:33:48,660
I was trying to target it first.

1528
01:33:52,780 --> 01:33:53,940
Oh yeah, it's way faster.

1529
01:33:54,500 --> 01:33:55,140
I think.

1530
01:33:55,980 --> 01:33:57,380
Can you jump over the big one?

1531
01:33:59,420 --> 01:33:59,980
Yeah!

1532
01:34:02,980 --> 01:34:04,060
There we go!

1533
01:34:06,700 --> 01:34:07,260
Again!

1534
01:34:09,840 --> 01:34:10,400
Beautiful!

1535
01:34:12,480 --> 01:34:13,300
So good!

1536
01:34:15,300 --> 01:34:16,440
Well done, Epona!

1537
01:34:16,780 --> 01:34:18,020
Can we make it too?

1538
01:34:18,580 --> 01:34:19,140
One!

1539
01:34:19,520 --> 01:34:20,080
No!

1540
01:34:20,860 --> 01:34:21,880
Okay, we're gonna try that again.

1541
01:34:22,040 --> 01:34:22,520
One more time.

1542
01:34:23,540 --> 01:34:24,000
One more time.

1543
01:34:25,360 --> 01:34:26,000
Check it out.

1544
01:34:28,760 --> 01:34:29,260
Yeah, yeah.

1545
01:34:29,360 --> 01:34:30,540
Just give me the spiel again.

1546
01:34:31,920 --> 01:34:32,480
It's fine.

1547
01:34:37,200 --> 01:34:38,180
Let's just get in quick.

1548
01:34:38,180 --> 01:34:39,100
And as soon as it starts running...

1549
01:34:40,840 --> 01:34:41,500
Does that work?

1550
01:34:41,600 --> 01:34:42,360
Maybe we're too far away.

1551
01:34:51,730 --> 01:34:52,470
Come on, come on, come on.

1552
01:34:56,950 --> 01:34:57,310
Go!

1553
01:35:02,770 --> 01:35:03,130
Jump.

1554
01:35:03,270 --> 01:35:03,730
Okay, nice.

1555
01:35:04,870 --> 01:35:06,130
Now we go around like this.

1556
01:35:10,520 --> 01:35:11,240
Oh, Epona!

1557
01:35:11,240 --> 01:35:11,360
Epona!

1558
01:35:12,320 --> 01:35:13,560
What the fuck?!

1559
01:35:15,580 --> 01:35:18,520
I played you the song and everything, and you failed me like this!

1560
01:35:24,640 --> 01:35:25,080
Turn.

1561
01:35:27,160 --> 01:35:27,740
Come on!

1562
01:35:28,040 --> 01:35:28,480
Yes!

1563
01:35:30,260 --> 01:35:31,720
I was about to say good dog.

1564
01:35:32,020 --> 01:35:32,800
I mean, good horse.

1565
01:35:33,060 --> 01:35:33,680
Good horsey.

1566
01:35:35,900 --> 01:35:36,520
One more.

1567
01:35:36,600 --> 01:35:37,220
Come on, come on, come on.

1568
01:35:40,510 --> 01:35:40,870
Go!

1569
01:35:41,610 --> 01:35:42,490
What the?!

1570
01:35:42,930 --> 01:35:43,370
Epona!

1571
01:35:44,450 --> 01:35:45,330
You suck!

1572
01:35:47,550 --> 01:35:48,690
Oh my god!

1573
01:35:50,690 --> 01:35:52,370
I'm gonna, I'm gonna become poor.

1574
01:35:55,230 --> 01:35:56,190
Uh, right.

1575
01:35:56,850 --> 01:35:57,790
Maybe I don't listen.

1576
01:35:58,910 --> 01:35:59,910
Thank you so much.

1577
01:36:01,190 --> 01:36:01,790
All right.

1578
01:36:02,770 --> 01:36:04,130
I don't even know what I'm trying to do.

1579
01:36:04,230 --> 01:36:05,270
I guess I'm trying to break a record.

1580
01:36:05,370 --> 01:36:06,490
Just like the fishing thing, right?

1581
01:36:10,460 --> 01:36:12,340
Maybe the small jump doesn't give any points.

1582
01:36:12,340 --> 01:36:14,840
It only feels like when I jump the big one, I get a little sound.

1583
01:36:25,900 --> 01:36:26,480
Come on!

1584
01:36:27,200 --> 01:36:27,960
Why are you so slow?

1585
01:36:31,870 --> 01:36:33,210
Also, I think I'm going the wrong way.

1586
01:36:33,390 --> 01:36:34,830
Uh, I'm making it harder on myself here.

1587
01:36:37,330 --> 01:36:38,270
The other way is better.

1588
01:36:40,050 --> 01:36:40,370
Beautiful.

1589
01:36:41,410 --> 01:36:41,970
But it's okay.

1590
01:36:42,010 --> 01:36:43,030
I'm just gonna keep going this way.

1591
01:36:44,330 --> 01:36:45,010
Because I'm a G.

1592
01:36:48,800 --> 01:36:49,380
Keep going.

1593
01:36:49,380 --> 01:36:52,320
Give ourselves some space here.

1594
01:36:55,350 --> 01:36:55,890
Yes!

1595
01:36:56,970 --> 01:36:57,510
Wonderful.

1596
01:37:02,340 --> 01:37:03,000
Nice.

1597
01:37:10,090 --> 01:37:10,630
Go!

1598
01:37:13,090 --> 01:37:14,870
I must have gotten some kind of record here.

1599
01:37:19,730 --> 01:37:20,710
Okay, maybe not.

1600
01:37:22,590 --> 01:37:23,130
Fine.

1601
01:37:25,150 --> 01:37:29,610
Can I access this pit without paying?

1602
01:37:31,070 --> 01:37:32,150
Or do I need to pay?

1603
01:37:36,250 --> 01:37:37,470
Guess I'm getting back later.

1604
01:37:37,630 --> 01:37:38,890
Oh, what are these chickens doing outside?

1605
01:37:40,390 --> 01:37:41,090
What the hell?

1606
01:37:43,910 --> 01:37:46,070
I tried to break it like you break the...

1607
01:37:46,070 --> 01:37:46,850
the jars.

1608
01:37:47,850 --> 01:37:49,250
You can't break a chicken.

1609
01:37:49,770 --> 01:37:50,590
I mean, you can.

1610
01:37:50,810 --> 01:37:53,150
But you shouldn't do that, I guess.

1611
01:37:55,550 --> 01:37:56,610
Oh, wait a minute.

1612
01:37:59,110 --> 01:37:59,550
Melon!

1613
01:38:03,390 --> 01:38:04,410
Tell me about the horse.

1614
01:38:05,670 --> 01:38:06,990
Uh, you're not gonna tell me anything?

1615
01:38:07,110 --> 01:38:07,330
Okay.

1616
01:38:07,970 --> 01:38:08,690
Oh, wait a minute.

1617
01:38:08,870 --> 01:38:09,330
Why are you...

1618
01:38:12,180 --> 01:38:13,080
I need to see that again.

1619
01:38:13,080 --> 01:38:13,320
Sorry.

1620
01:38:15,080 --> 01:38:17,220
Can I just skip one at a time instead of everything?

1621
01:38:20,370 --> 01:38:21,410
Uh, let's see here.

1622
01:38:26,970 --> 01:38:29,270
I'm using the ranch to gain Ganondorf's favor.

1623
01:38:30,330 --> 01:38:32,330
I think she wants me to do something with Ingo.

1624
01:38:34,850 --> 01:38:36,830
He was kicked out of the ranch by Mr. Ingo.

1625
01:38:38,030 --> 01:38:39,510
If I disobey, he will treat...

1626
01:38:39,510 --> 01:38:40,410
That is so horrible.

1627
01:38:40,910 --> 01:38:41,690
Mr. Ingo sucks.

1628
01:38:44,370 --> 01:38:45,990
I don't want him to treat the horses badly.

1629
01:38:46,130 --> 01:38:46,770
Can I just kill him?

1630
01:38:48,430 --> 01:38:50,470
I'll be back later and rescue all the horses.

1631
01:38:50,690 --> 01:38:51,390
I swear to...

1632
01:38:51,390 --> 01:38:52,110
I swear it.

1633
01:38:57,130 --> 01:38:59,770
I really thought I could get a horse there and actually ride it.

1634
01:39:00,210 --> 01:39:01,270
Like the intro, right?

1635
01:39:02,390 --> 01:39:03,270
Maybe I can later.

1636
01:39:04,230 --> 01:39:05,010
Uh, cheers.

1637
01:39:09,590 --> 01:39:11,250
Now I'm gonna go up to Kakariko.

1638
01:39:13,050 --> 01:39:13,690
Hell yeah.

1639
01:39:14,510 --> 01:39:15,650
I've got business there.

1640
01:39:16,270 --> 01:39:18,470
Hopefully I can increase the size of my coin pouch.

1641
01:39:19,070 --> 01:39:20,890
That is the number one thing right now.

1642
01:39:22,430 --> 01:39:24,410
Because I want to be spending my money.

1643
01:39:35,660 --> 01:39:37,780
I think it's trying to simulate a wolf.

1644
01:39:39,060 --> 01:39:39,540
However...

1645
01:39:41,160 --> 01:39:43,040
That's not what that sounds like.

1646
01:39:44,240 --> 01:39:45,040
It's horrible.

1647
01:39:45,040 --> 01:39:46,980
I don't know what that sound is.

1648
01:39:48,140 --> 01:39:49,300
It is not that.

1649
01:39:52,580 --> 01:39:54,320
Okay, so what about this weird tree here?

1650
01:39:59,060 --> 01:39:59,700
Money me.

1651
01:40:03,760 --> 01:40:05,980
Dude, I want to go to the windmill again just to hear that song.

1652
01:40:11,860 --> 01:40:12,760
Come on, baby.

1653
01:40:14,620 --> 01:40:15,200
Let's see.

1654
01:40:17,540 --> 01:40:18,480
You have been freed.

1655
01:40:18,680 --> 01:40:19,120
What about you?

1656
01:40:22,290 --> 01:40:26,130
Since you've destroyed 21 spiders of the curse, the curse is starting to weaken.

1657
01:40:26,930 --> 01:40:29,530
Did the kids who returned to normal give you any rewards?

1658
01:40:30,610 --> 01:40:31,130
No!

1659
01:40:31,610 --> 01:40:32,650
I don't have enough?

1660
01:40:33,130 --> 01:40:33,930
Oh, wait, wait.

1661
01:40:35,270 --> 01:40:36,770
The curse has been broken!

1662
01:40:37,050 --> 01:40:37,730
Thank you!

1663
01:40:38,010 --> 01:40:39,210
Here's a reward for you.

1664
01:40:42,050 --> 01:40:43,690
You obtained the stone of agony?

1665
01:40:44,590 --> 01:40:47,970
If you equip a rumble pack, it will react to nearby secrets.

1666
01:40:49,630 --> 01:40:51,630
Oh my god, I don't have that.

1667
01:40:54,420 --> 01:40:56,020
I wonder how that's gonna work.

1668
01:40:57,400 --> 01:41:00,200
Wait, is there a rumble in this?

1669
01:41:00,400 --> 01:41:01,460
I haven't paid attention.

1670
01:41:03,620 --> 01:41:05,180
Oh my god, no!

1671
01:41:06,180 --> 01:41:07,740
I'm gonna be missing secrets!

1672
01:41:13,200 --> 01:41:14,180
Oh no!

1673
01:41:19,350 --> 01:41:21,090
Can I actually use it somehow?

1674
01:41:25,460 --> 01:41:26,480
Oh, it's there.

1675
01:41:28,020 --> 01:41:29,180
Stone of agony.

1676
01:41:33,020 --> 01:41:36,580
It looks like a rumble pack for a Nintendo 64 controller.

1677
01:41:37,140 --> 01:41:38,220
That's kind of funny.

1678
01:41:41,850 --> 01:41:42,410
Okay.

1679
01:41:44,570 --> 01:41:47,130
Now the question is, can I destroy these boxes with this?

1680
01:41:48,150 --> 01:41:49,170
I can't.

1681
01:41:49,410 --> 01:41:50,230
What about this?

1682
01:41:51,990 --> 01:41:52,550
No.

1683
01:41:52,910 --> 01:41:54,750
Why can I not destroy it with my sword?

1684
01:41:56,730 --> 01:41:58,530
Like, I don't want to be wasting bombs on that.

1685
01:41:59,050 --> 01:42:02,870
So there's stuff down here, but I want to go visit Talon.

1686
01:42:03,610 --> 01:42:04,190
Malon's dad.

1687
01:42:04,730 --> 01:42:06,210
And see what he's up to.

1688
01:42:06,330 --> 01:42:11,010
Maybe give him some information about the state of affairs back in Lon Lon Ranch.

1689
01:42:11,630 --> 01:42:13,470
And the inevitable torture of the horses.

1690
01:42:14,010 --> 01:42:14,930
Which is very sad.

1691
01:42:15,110 --> 01:42:15,990
Also, it's not down here.

1692
01:42:16,170 --> 01:42:16,630
I mean, up there.

1693
01:42:16,710 --> 01:42:17,130
It's down here.

1694
01:42:18,790 --> 01:42:19,430
Here it is.

